1276450	Requirement	Move PNC Indicator from Account to (PLT or PL)			Ready for Solution	Proposed	Kothapalli, Prashanth (CW) <Prashanth.Kothapalli@ibx.com>		IHG	BX; Credentialing; DART; Go Live; NR	311036733	7803	IHG\BTS EIM\PNM\Sprint 53	9725	IHG\BTS EIM\Provider Network Management		<div style="box-sizing:border-box;flex:1 1 0%;min-width:0px;margin-bottom:0px;color:rgb(24, 24, 24);font-family:-apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, &quot;Segoe UI&quot;, Roboto, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif, &quot;Apple Color Emoji&quot;, &quot;Segoe UI Emoji&quot;, &quot;Segoe UI Symbol&quot;;font-size:13px;background-color:rgb(243, 243, 243);"><h1 style="box-sizing:border-box;font-size:1em;margin:0px;"> </h1> </div><ul><li><span><b>Field Configuration (moving from Account to PLT)</b></span> </li><li><b>Editable Fields:</b> </li><ul><li>Remove from Account </li><li>Add to PL or PLT </li> </ul><li>Practitioner Participation → PNC Logic is moved to PLT </li><ul><li>Check Practice Locations → Check Practice Location Taxonomy </li><ul><li>Assumption – If Practitioner is bringing a new Taxonomy, it is not PNC </li><li>If Existing PLT &amp; PNC = TRUE → Then PNC </li> </ul> </ul><li><b>Regression: </b> </li><ul><li>Provider Change Request </li><li>PDM Manual Changes </li> </ul><li><b>Data Load Impact:</b> </li><ul><li>Re-Load PNC on PLT </li> </ul> </ul><span></span><br><br>																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																							
1396629	Requirement	PNC - PDM Manual Updates Guided Flow - Vendor ( Add / Remove PNC ) -> Practice Location  ( Add / Remove PNC )			Approved by PO	Proposed	Kothapalli, Prashanth (CW) <Prashanth.Kothapalli@ibx.com>		IHG	BX; Credentialing; Go Live; NR	311036733	7803	IHG\BTS EIM\PNM\Sprint 53	9725	IHG\BTS EIM\Provider Network Management		<div style="box-sizing:border-box;flex:1 1 0%;min-width:0px;margin-bottom:0px;color:rgb(24, 24, 24);font-family:-apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, &quot;Segoe UI&quot;, Roboto, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif, &quot;Apple Color Emoji&quot;, &quot;Segoe UI Emoji&quot;, &quot;Segoe UI Symbol&quot;;font-size:13px;background-color:rgb(243, 243, 243);"><h1 style="box-sizing:border-box;font-size:1em;margin:0px;"> </h1> </div><span style="font-weight:bold;">⚠️ Pending Business Decisions (Required Before Development)<br></span><div style="font-weight:bold;">Before the UI changes can be finalized, the business must confirm the following:<br> </div><div style="font-weight:bold;"><br> </div><div style="font-weight:bold;">Flow Placement (Request Type): Should the &quot;Add/Remove PNC&quot; option remain under the Vendor manual update path, be moved to the Practice Location manual update path? <span style="background-color:rgb(0, 255, 0);">Moved to Practice Location</span><br> </div><div style="font-weight:bold;"><br> </div><div><b>AC1: UI – NPI Search and Multi-Location Display</b> </div><div><b><br></b><div><b>Given </b>the PDM Specialist is using the PDM manual updates flow to Add/Remove PNC,<br> </div><div><br> </div><div><b>When </b>they search for practice locations (based on the pending business decision for search criteria),<br> </div><div><br> </div><div><b></b> </div><span><b>Then </b>the system shall fetch and display all practice locations associated with that NPI.<br></span><div><br> </div><div><ul><li>The display shall be a table with one row per location. (Multi Selection) </li><li><span>Each row shall display the Location Name, Address and an editable PNC checkbox.</span> </li> </ul> </div><div><ul><li>Checking the box indicates &quot;Add PNC&quot; (true) and unchecking indicates &quot;Remove PNC&quot; (false). </li> </ul><div><span><b>AC2: Validation – at least one PNC location must be changed</b></span> </div><div><span><b><br></b></span><div><b></b> </div><span><b>Given </b>the PDM Specialist has viewed the Add/Remove PNC step with all locations displayed based on the NPI search,<br></span><div><br> </div><div><b>When </b>they attempt to submit without changing the PNC checkbox for any location (i.e., all checkbox values match their original states),<br> </div><div><br> </div><div><b>Then </b>the system shall display the error &quot;At least one PNC location must be changed before submit.&quot;<br> </div><span><b>And </b>the system shall block the submit action, requiring the user to change at least one location's PNC value to proceed.</span><span></span><br> </div><div><span><br></span> </div><div><b style="box-sizing:border-box;">Technical Implementation Details For Dev Team</b><br style="box-sizing:border-box;"><br> </div><div><span><b>AC3: OmniScript &amp; Data Flow Updates (Technical)</b><br></span><div><b>Given</b> the PDM Specialist multi-selects facilities and sets the PNC checkbox for each row,<br> </div><div><br> </div><div><b>When </b>the OmniScript (PRM_PDMManualUpdate_English) processes the submission,<br> </div><div><br> </div><div><b>Then </b>the flow shall update HealthcareFacility.PRM_PNC__c (not Account.PRM_PNC__c).<br> </div><div><br> </div><div><ul><li>SV_PNC must be modified to pass an array of FacilitiesToUpdate containing the HealthcareFacilityId (RecordId) and isPNC value for each row. </li><li>The IP PRM_PDMRecordsCreation shall route the payload to a new or modified DataRaptor (e.g., PRMDRUpdateHealthcareFacilityPNC or PRMLoadFacilityLocAddUpdate) capable of processing batch updates to the HealthcareFacility object. </li><li>The execution of PRMDRUpdateAccountPDM (which updates Account PNC) shall be disabled or bypassed for the &quot;Add/Remove PNC&quot; update type. </li> </ul> </div><div><br> </div><div><b>AC4: Apex – HealthcareFacility Trigger (Technical)</b><br> </div><div><b>Given </b>HealthcareFacility.PRM_PNC__c is updated directly or via the OmniScript flow,<br> </div><div><br> </div><div><b>When </b>the record is saved to the database,<br> </div><div><br> </div><div><b>Then </b>a new trigger on HealthcareFacility shall fire on after insert and after update.<br> </div><div><br> </div><div><ul><li>It shall identify records where PRM_PNC__c has changed. </li><li>It shall query HealthcarePractitionerFacility to find all active affiliations (RecordType.DeveloperName = 'PRM_PractitionerLocationAffiliation') linked to the changed locations. </li><li>It shall recalculate PNC for all collected PractitionerIds using the &quot;any&quot; logic (if any location is PNC, the practitioner is PNC). </li><li>It shall update the Practitioner Account (PersonContactId → Account) with the new PRM_PNC__c value. </li> </ul> </div><div><br> </div><div>The code must be bulkified, handling multiple facility updates in a single transaction without DML/SOQL in loops.<br> </div><div><br> </div> </div> </div> </div><div style="font-weight:bold;"><br> </div>																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																							
1396749	Requirement	PNC - RCAT Guided flow updates			Approved by PO	Proposed	Kothapalli, Prashanth (CW) <Prashanth.Kothapalli@ibx.com>		IHG	BX; Credentialing; Go Live; NR	311036733	7803	IHG\BTS EIM\PNM\Sprint 53	9725	IHG\BTS EIM\Provider Network Management		<div style="box-sizing:border-box;flex:1 1 0%;min-width:0px;margin-bottom:0px;color:rgb(24, 24, 24);font-family:-apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, &quot;Segoe UI&quot;, Roboto, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif, &quot;Apple Color Emoji&quot;, &quot;Segoe UI Emoji&quot;, &quot;Segoe UI Symbol&quot;;font-size:13px;background-color:rgb(243, 243, 243);"><h1 style="box-sizing:border-box;font-size:1em;margin:0px;"> </h1> </div><div><i>RCAT is the process for reviewing practitioners due for recredentialing who are flagged for termination. The guided flow contains three steps that must be updated to display practice location PNC (HealthcareFacility.PRM_PNC__c) instead of the deprecated vendor PNC (Account.PRM_PNC__c):<br></i> </div><div><i><br></i> </div><div><i><b>Step 1 (Review PNC &amp; Delegated)</b>: Displays practitioners with PNC/Delegated locations. The code must be updated to consume PNC from Account.PRM_PNC__c<br></i> </div><div><i><br></i> </div><div><i><b>Step 2 (Review Last Man Standing)</b>: Displays LMS practitioners. PRM_RCATProcessingHelper must be updated to set loc.pnc from HealthcareFacility.PRM_PNC__c.<br></i> </div><div><i><br></i> </div><span><i><b>Step 3 (Not Last AND PNC Delegated)</b>: Displays practitioners with at least one other active practitioner at their locations. DataRaptors must be updated to supply HealthcareFacility.PRM_PNC__c</i></span><div><span><i><br></i></span> </div><div><span><i><br></i></span> </div><div><span><b>AC1: Correct PNC Display Across All Steps</b></span> </div><div><span><b><br></b><div><b>Given </b>the Credentialing Specialist uses the RCAT guided flow to review recredentialing terminations,<br> </div><div><br> </div><div><b>When </b>they view Step 1 (Review PNC &amp; Delegated), Step 2 (Review Last Man Standing), or Step 3 (Review RCAT – Not Last AND PNC Delegated),<br> </div><div><br> </div><div><b>Then </b>the PNC checkbox for each practitioner/location row shall accurately display the value from HealthcareFacility.PRM_PNC__c (practice location PNC), not the deprecated Account.PRM_PNC__c.<br> </div><div><br> </div>The Custom LWCs (CustomLWC1, CustomLWC2, CustomLWC3) rendering these tables must consume the updated PNC payload from their respective data sources (DataRaptors or PracLoc.pnc from Apex).<br></span><div><br><br> </div> </div>																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																							
1396793	Requirement	PNC & Delegated - PDM Manual Updates Guided Flow - Practice Location			Approved by PO	Proposed	Kothapalli, Prashanth (CW) <Prashanth.Kothapalli@ibx.com>		IHG	BX; Credentialing; Go Live; NR	311036733	7803	IHG\BTS EIM\PNM\Sprint 53	9725	IHG\BTS EIM\Provider Network Management		<div style="box-sizing:border-box;flex:1 1 0%;min-width:0px;margin-bottom:0px;color:rgb(24, 24, 24);font-family:-apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, &quot;Segoe UI&quot;, Roboto, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif, &quot;Apple Color Emoji&quot;, &quot;Segoe UI Emoji&quot;, &quot;Segoe UI Symbol&quot;;font-size:13px;background-color:rgb(243, 243, 243);"><h1 style="box-sizing:border-box;font-size:1em;margin:0px;"> </h1> </div><b>Business Context (The &quot;Why&quot;)</b><div><b><br></b><span>Currently, when a user selects a practice location in the PDM flow, the &quot;PNC (Par Non Cred)&quot; checkbox shown on the screen actually reads the status of the overall Vendor Account (the parent group). Because we are moving PNC tracking to the individual location level, this UI element must be updated.</span><br> </div><div><span><br></span> </div><div><span><span><b>AC1: Displaying PNC in the &quot;Practice Location&quot; Path</b></span></span> </div><div><span><span><b><br></b></span><div><b>Given </b>the PDM Specialist is using the PDM Manual Update flow and selects the &quot;Practice Location&quot; path for any relevant request type (such as Add/Remove a Practitioner, Update Office Hours, Add/Remove Network, etc.),<br> </div><div><br> </div><div><b>When </b>they search for a group and select a specific practice location from the search results,<br> </div><div><br> </div><span><b>Then </b>the &quot;Selected Practice Location&quot; summary block shall display a PNC (Par Non Cred) checkbox that accurately reflects the specific practice location's actual PNC status, rather than the parent vendor's status.</span><br></span> </div><div><span><span><br></span></span> </div><div><span><span><b style="box-sizing:border-box;">Technical Implementation Details For Dev Team</b><br></span></span> </div><div><span><span><b style="box-sizing:border-box;"><br></b></span></span> </div><div><span><span><span><b></b></span></span></span> </div><span><b>AC2: Execute Practitioner Verification Rules (PNCValid &amp; DelegatedValid)</b></span><div><span><b><br></b></span><div><b>Given </b>the PDM Specialist submits a request to add or remove a practitioner,<br> </div><div><br> </div><div><b>When </b>the system runs practitioner verification (PRM_VerifyPractitionerDetails),<br> </div><div><br> </div><div><b>Then </b>the system shall validate using the updated location-level PNC and practitioner delegated statuses: </div><ul><li><span>If the selected location is Delegated, <span style="box-sizing:border-box;background-color:rgb(255, 255, 0);">Practitioner can be&nbsp;</span><span style="box-sizing:border-box;background-color:rgb(255, 255, 0);">Delegated, PNC or Cred</span></span> </li> </ul><div><span><span><span><br></span><br></span><span style="background-color:rgb(255, 255, 0);">original user story </span><span><a href="https://1901market.visualstudio.com/IHG/_workitems/edit/925777/" data-vss-mention="version:1.0"><span style="background-color:rgb(255, 255, 0);">#925777</span></a></span><span style="background-color:rgb(255, 255, 0);"> </span><span><br><ul style="box-sizing:border-box;padding:0px 0px 0px 40px;"><li style="box-sizing:border-box;"><span style="background-color:rgb(255, 255, 0);">Practitioner found:</span> </li><ul style="box-sizing:border-box;padding:0px 0px 0px 40px;"><li style="box-sizing:border-box;"><span style="box-sizing:border-box;background-color:rgb(255, 255, 0);">If Practitioner is</span><span style="box-sizing:border-box;"><span style="box-sizing:border-box;background-color:rgb(255, 255, 0);">&nbsp;(Any&nbsp;</span></span><span style="box-sizing:border-box;background-color:rgb(255, 255, 0);">PNC)</span><span style="box-sizing:border-box;background-color:rgb(255, 192, 128);"><span style="box-sizing:border-box;background-color:rgb(255, 255, 0);">&nbsp;</span></span><span style="box-sizing:border-box;background-color:rgb(255, 255, 0);">&amp; Practice Location is</span><span style="box-sizing:border-box;"><span style="box-sizing:border-box;background-color:rgb(255, 255, 0);">&nbsp;</span></span><span style="box-sizing:border-box;background-color:rgb(255, 255, 0);">PNC&nbsp;</span><span style="box-sizing:border-box;background-color:rgb(255, 255, 0);">--&gt; Can Proceed</span><br style="box-sizing:border-box;"> </li><li style="box-sizing:border-box;"><span style="box-sizing:border-box;background-color:rgb(255, 255, 0);">If Practitioner</span><span style="box-sizing:border-box;"><span style="box-sizing:border-box;background-color:rgb(255, 255, 0);">&nbsp;(</span></span><span style="box-sizing:border-box;background-color:rgb(255, 255, 0);">PNC Only)&nbsp;</span><span style="box-sizing:border-box;background-color:rgb(255, 255, 0);">&amp; Practice Location is not</span><span style="box-sizing:border-box;"><span style="box-sizing:border-box;background-color:rgb(255, 255, 0);">&nbsp;</span></span><span style="box-sizing:border-box;background-color:rgb(255, 255, 0);">PNC&nbsp;</span><span style="box-sizing:border-box;background-color:rgb(255, 255, 0);">--&gt; Error Message</span><br style="box-sizing:border-box;"> </li><ul style="box-sizing:border-box;padding:0px 0px 0px 40px;"><li style="box-sizing:border-box;"><span style="box-sizing:border-box;background-color:rgb(255, 255, 0);">This Practitioner is not found in our system, please submit the</span><span style="box-sizing:border-box;background-color:rgb(255, 255, 0);">&nbsp;</span><span style="box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(12, 100, 192);background-color:rgb(255, 255, 0);">Practitioner Participation Form.</span> </li><ul style="box-sizing:border-box;padding:0px 0px 0px 40px;"><li style="box-sizing:border-box;"><span style="box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(12, 100, 192);background-color:rgb(255, 255, 0);">Hyperlink to Practitioner Participation Form</span><span style="box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(12, 100, 192);"></span> </li> </ul> </ul> </ul><ul style="box-sizing:border-box;padding:0px 0px 0px 40px;"><li style="box-sizing:border-box;"><span style="box-sizing:border-box;background-color:rgb(255, 255, 0);">If Practitioner is</span><span style="box-sizing:border-box;"><span style="box-sizing:border-box;background-color:rgb(255, 255, 0);">&nbsp;</span></span><span style="box-sizing:border-box;background-color:rgb(255, 255, 0);">Delegated</span><span style="box-sizing:border-box;background-color:rgb(128, 255, 255);"><span style="box-sizing:border-box;background-color:rgb(255, 255, 0);">&nbsp;</span></span><span style="box-sizing:border-box;background-color:rgb(255, 255, 0);">&amp; Location is</span><span style="box-sizing:border-box;"><span style="box-sizing:border-box;background-color:rgb(255, 255, 0);">&nbsp;</span></span><span style="box-sizing:border-box;background-color:rgb(255, 255, 0);">Delegated&nbsp;</span><span style="box-sizing:border-box;background-color:rgb(255, 255, 0);">--&gt; Can Proceed</span><br style="box-sizing:border-box;"> </li><li style="box-sizing:border-box;"><span style="box-sizing:border-box;background-color:rgb(255, 255, 0);">If Practitioner (</span><span style="box-sizing:border-box;background-color:rgb(255, 255, 0);">Delegated Only)&nbsp;</span><span style="box-sizing:border-box;background-color:rgb(255, 255, 0);">&amp; Practice location is not</span><span style="box-sizing:border-box;"><span style="box-sizing:border-box;background-color:rgb(255, 255, 0);">&nbsp;</span></span><span style="box-sizing:border-box;background-color:rgb(255, 255, 0);">Delegated&nbsp;</span><span style="box-sizing:border-box;background-color:rgb(255, 255, 0);">--&gt; Error Message</span><br style="box-sizing:border-box;"> </li><ul style="box-sizing:border-box;padding:0px 0px 0px 40px;"><li style="box-sizing:border-box;"><span style="box-sizing:border-box;background-color:rgb(255, 255, 0);">This Practitioner is not found in our system, please submit the</span><span style="box-sizing:border-box;background-color:rgb(255, 255, 0);">&nbsp;</span><span style="box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(12, 100, 192);background-color:rgb(255, 255, 0);">Practitioner Participation Form.</span><br style="box-sizing:border-box;"> </li><ul style="box-sizing:border-box;padding:0px 0px 0px 40px;"><li style="box-sizing:border-box;"><span style="box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(12, 100, 192);display:inline !important;"><span style="box-sizing:border-box;background-color:rgb(255, 255, 0);">Hyperlink to Practitioner Participation Form</span></span> </li> </ul> </ul> </ul> </ul><br></span></span> </div><div><span><span><br></span></span> </div><div><span><span><br></span></span> </div> </div>																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																							
1396794	Requirement	PNC - Data Model – Deprecate PNC on Vendor Account			Approved by PO	Proposed	Kothapalli, Prashanth (CW) <Prashanth.Kothapalli@ibx.com>		IHG	BX; Credentialing; DART; Go Live; NR	311036733	7803	IHG\BTS EIM\PNM\Sprint 53	9725	IHG\BTS EIM\Provider Network Management		<div style="box-sizing:border-box;flex:1 1 0%;min-width:0px;margin-bottom:0px;color:rgb(24, 24, 24);font-family:-apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, &quot;Segoe UI&quot;, Roboto, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif, &quot;Apple Color Emoji&quot;, &quot;Segoe UI Emoji&quot;, &quot;Segoe UI Symbol&quot;;font-size:13px;background-color:rgb(243, 243, 243);"><h1 style="box-sizing:border-box;font-size:1em;margin:0px;"> </h1> </div><b>AC1: Confirm No Remaining References</b><div><b><br></b><div><b>Given </b>all Apex code, DataRaptors, Integration Procedures, and OmniScripts have been successfully updated and tested (<span style="background-color:rgb(255, 255, 0);">PNC user stories - Sprint 53 </span>),<br> </div><div><br> </div><div><b>When </b>the Admin or Developer runs a global search for Account.PRM_PNC__c and PRM_PNC__c specifically in the context of the Vendor Account,<br> </div><div><br> </div><div><b>Then </b>there shall be zero remaining references that write to or read from the Vendor Account.PRM_PNC__c field for practice location PNC.<br> </div><div><br> </div><div>Note: The PRM_PNC__c field on the Practitioner Account (which acts as a rollup) must remain intact and is exempt from this cleanup.<br> </div><div><br> </div><div><b>AC2: Remove or Hide the Field</b><br> </div><div><b><br></b> </div><div><b>Given </b>it is confirmed that no active system components reference the Vendor Account PNC field,<br> </div><div><br> </div><div><b>When </b>the Admin modifies the Salesforce UI and schema,<br> </div><div><br> </div><div><b>Then </b>the PRM_PNC__c field shall be removed from the Vendor Account page layouts so it is no longer visible or editable by any users.<br> </div><div><br> </div><div><ul><li>If the field is fully deleted from the object schema, the Admin must first ensure no external integrations or managed packages depend on it. </li> </ul> </div><div><br> </div><div><b>AC3: System Documentation</b><br> </div><div><b><br></b> </div><div><b>Given </b>the field deprecation and UI cleanup is complete,<br> </div><div><br> </div><div><b>When </b>the Admin updates the project's data dictionary and release notes,<br> </div><div><br> </div><div><b>Then </b>the documentation shall explicitly state two things:<br> </div><div><br> </div><div><ul><li>PNC is now managed exclusively on the HealthcareFacility (practice location) object. </li><li><span>The practitioner Account.PRM_PNC__c field is a rollup indicating if any of their affiliated locations are PNC = true.</span> </li> </ul><div><br> </div><div><span style="background-color:rgb(255, 255, 0);">If an account has only one location, then PNC is checked on that location during data migration</span> </div> </div> </div>																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																							
