1397504	Requirement	PNC & Delegated - Off-Cycle Credentialing			Approved by PO	Proposed	Kothapalli, Prashanth (CW) <Prashanth.Kothapalli@ibx.com>		IHG	BX; Credentialing; DART; Go Live; NR	325041747	7803	IHG\BTS EIM\PNM\Sprint 53	9725	IHG\BTS EIM\Provider Network Management		<div style="box-sizing:border-box;flex:1 1 0%;min-width:0px;margin-bottom:0px;color:rgb(24, 24, 24);font-family:-apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, &quot;Segoe UI&quot;, Roboto, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif, &quot;Apple Color Emoji&quot;, &quot;Segoe UI Emoji&quot;, &quot;Segoe UI Symbol&quot;;font-size:13px;background-color:rgb(243, 243, 243);"><h1 style="box-sizing:border-box;font-size:1em;margin:0px;"> </h1> </div><b></b><span><b>AC1: Block Delegated Practitioners</b></span><div><span><b><br></b></span><div><b>Given </b>the Credentialing Specialist searches for a provider in the Off-Cycle flow,<br> </div><div><br> </div><div><b>When </b>the practitioner is associated with all delegated practice locations (IsPractitionerDelegated = true),<br> </div><div><br> </div><div><b>And </b>their credentialing status is not &quot;Denied&quot;,<br> </div><div><br> </div><div><b>Then </b>the SetErrorForDelegatedPractitioner element shall block progression.<br> </div><div><ul><li>And the system shall display the error message: &quot;Practitioner must be fully credentialed, please submit a Practitioner Participation Request&quot;. </li><li><span>Conversely, when the provider has no delegated locations (IsPractitionerDelegated = false), they shall be allowed to proceed.</span> </li> </ul> </div><div><br><div><span><b></b></span> </div><span><b>AC2: Display Facility-Level PNC</b></span> </div><div><span><b><br></b></span><div><b>Given </b>the Credentialing Specialist successfully searches for a non-delegated provider,<br> </div><div><br> </div><div><b>When </b>they view the provider search results,<br> </div><div><br> </div><span><b>Then </b>the PNC value displayed for each individual facility shall be sourced directly from HealthcareFacility.PRM_PNC__c.</span><blockquote style="margin:0 0 0 40px;border:none;"><div><span></span> </div></blockquote><span></span><br><br> </div> </div>																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																							
1394622	Requirement	PNC - Practitioner Participation Form			Approved by PO	Proposed	Kothapalli, Prashanth (CW) <Prashanth.Kothapalli@ibx.com>		IHG	BX; Credentialing; Go Live; NR	339046761	7803	IHG\BTS EIM\PNM\Sprint 53	9725	IHG\BTS EIM\Provider Network Management		<div style="box-sizing:border-box;flex:1 1 0%;min-width:0px;margin-bottom:0px;color:rgb(24, 24, 24);font-family:-apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, &quot;Segoe UI&quot;, Roboto, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif, &quot;Apple Color Emoji&quot;, &quot;Segoe UI Emoji&quot;, &quot;Segoe UI Symbol&quot;;font-size:13px;background-color:rgb(243, 243, 243);"><h1 style="box-sizing:border-box;font-size:1em;margin:0px;"> </h1> </div><b>AC1: PNC determination – change from &quot;all groups PNC&quot; to &quot;any practice location PNC&quot;</b><div><b><br></b><blockquote style="margin:0 0 0 40px;border:none;"><div><b>Given </b>the Practitioner Participation Form (PRM_PractitionerParticipationForm_English) is used to onboard PNC practitioners, </div></blockquote><div><br> </div> </div><blockquote style="margin:0 0 0 40px;border:none;"><div><div><b>And </b>the flow currently checks if the practitioner is joining PNC-only accounts (groups) and sets the practitioner's PNC checkbox accordingly; the case manager created after submission uses Record Type &quot;PNC&quot; when the practitioner is PNC, </div> </div></blockquote><div><div><br> </div> </div><blockquote style="margin:0 0 0 40px;border:none;"><div><div><b>When </b>the developer updates the flow for the new data model (PNC on practice location), </div> </div></blockquote><div><div><br> </div> </div><blockquote style="margin:0 0 0 40px;border:none;"><div><div><b>Then </b>the logic shall change as follows: </div> </div></blockquote><blockquote style="margin:0 0 0 40px;border:none;"><ul><li>For each practice location, read HealthcareFacility.PRM_PNC__c. </li><li>If any one of the practice locations the practitioner is joining has PRM_PNC__c = true, then set the practitioner's PNC checkbox to true (PNCFlag = true). </li><li><span style="background-color:rgb(0, 255, 0);">When all the locations practitioner joining are PNC , the case manager created after submission shall use Record Type PNC.</span> </li><li>When no practice location are PNC, the case manager shall use the Practitioner Participation record type. </li> </ul><div><div><b>Current behavior (for reference):</b> </div> </div><ul><li>Groups selected in the flow have a pnc property from the vendor Account (Account.PRM_PNC__c). </li><li>SV_PNCFlag (PRM_PractitionerScreenRecordCreation) filters GroupInformation for pnc = false. </li><li>PNCFlag is derived: practitioner is PNC only when all groups they join have pnc = true (i.e., practitioner joins PNC-only accounts). </li><li>PRMDRCreateCaseCaseManagerAndAccount uses PNCFlag to set Account.PRM_PNC__c on the practitioner and to set the IndividualApplication RecordType to PNC <br><br> </li> </ul></blockquote><div><b>Technical Implementation Details For Dev Team</b><br><br><b>AC2: PRM_PractitionerScreenRecordCreation – SV_PNCFlag and PNCFlag formula<br></b><br> </div><blockquote style="margin:0 0 0 40px;border:none;"><div><div><b>Given </b>SV_PNCFlag filters GroupInformation for pnc = false and uses PNCFalseFlagList, </div> </div><div><div><br> </div> </div><div><div><b>When </b>the developer updates the Integration Procedure, </div> </div><div><div><br> </div> </div><div><div><b>Then </b>the logic shall evaluate practice locations (HealthcareFacilities) instead of groups (Accounts). </div> </div></blockquote><blockquote style="margin:0 0 0 40px;border:none;"><div><div><ul><li>The GroupInformation structure may need to include practice location data with HealthcareFacility.PRM_PNC__c, or a separate IP/DataRaptor must fetch practice locations for the selected groups and return a consolidated PNC flag (true if any location is PNC). </li><li>The PNCFlag formula passed to PRMDRCreateCaseCaseManagerAndAccount shall be: true if any practice location has PNC = true; false otherwise. </li> </ul> </div> </div></blockquote><b>AC3: PRM_IPExtractGroupNameBasedOnTINNPI – Apex and DataRaptors</b><div><b><br></b><blockquote style="margin:0 0 0 40px;border:none;"><div><div><b>Given </b>the IP fetches group data via Remote Actions RAGetUniqueGroupsForPNCTaxIdNPI and RAGetUniqueGroupsForTaxIdNPI (both call PRM_RecordQueryServiceUtils.getGroupDataForTaxIdNPI), </div> </div><div><div><br> </div> </div><div><div><b>And </b>the DataRaptor PRMDRExtractGroupNameBasedOnTINNPIPNC may be used in other contexts and maps Account.PRM_PNC__c → Account:PNC, </div> </div><div><div><br> </div> </div><div><div><b>When </b>the developer updates the group data source for PNC removal from Account, </div> </div></blockquote><div><div><br> </div> </div> </div><blockquote style="margin:0 0 0 40px;border:none;"><div><div><div><b>Then</b>: </div> </div> </div></blockquote><blockquote style="margin:0 0 0 40px;border:none;"><div><div><ul><li>Apex: PRM_RecordQueryServiceUtils.getAccount and getAccountWrapperData must derive the group-level PNC from HealthcareFacility.PRM_PNC__c (true if any practice location under the group has PNC = true) instead of reading Account.PRM_PNC__c. </li><li>DataRaptor (if used): PRMDRExtractGroupNameBasedOnTINNPIPNC must be updated to derive PNC from HealthcareFacility instead of Account. </li><li>The GroupInformation structure used by SV_PNCFlag must support the new evaluation (pnc = true when any practice location under the group is PNC). </li> </ul> </div> </div></blockquote><div><div><div><br> </div><div><b>AC4: PRMDRCreateCaseCaseManagerAndAccount – no structural change</b><br> </div> </div> </div><div><b><br></b> </div><blockquote style="margin:0 0 0 40px;border:none;"><div><div><div><b>Given </b>the DataRaptor receives PNCFlag and writes to Account.PRM_PNC__c and sets IndividualApplication RecordType, </div> </div> </div><div><div><div><br> </div> </div> </div><div><div><div><b>When </b>the developer reviews the DataRaptor, </div> </div> </div><div><div><div><br> </div> </div> </div><div><div><div><b>Then </b>no change to the DataRaptor input/output structure is required. </div> </div> </div></blockquote><blockquote style="margin:0 0 0 40px;border:none;"><div><div><ul><li>The PNCFlag value is computed differently upstream (AC1–AC3). </li><li>The DataRaptor continues to receive PNCFlag and write Account.PRM_PNC__c (practitioner) and set case type based on PNCFlag. </li> </ul> </div> </div></blockquote><div><blockquote style="margin:0 0 0 40px;border:none;"><br></blockquote> </div>																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																							
1394596	Requirement	PNC - Data Model – Data Migration For PNC at Practice Location			Ready for Grooming	Proposed	Kothapalli, Prashanth (CW) <Prashanth.Kothapalli@ibx.com>		IHG	BX; Credentialing; DART; Go Live; NR	353051775	7803	IHG\BTS EIM\PNM\Sprint 53	9725	IHG\BTS EIM\Provider Network Management		<div style="box-sizing:border-box;flex:1 1 0%;min-width:0px;margin-bottom:0px;color:rgb(24, 24, 24);font-family:-apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, &quot;Segoe UI&quot;, Roboto, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif, &quot;Apple Color Emoji&quot;, &quot;Segoe UI Emoji&quot;, &quot;Segoe UI Symbol&quot;;font-size:13px;background-color:rgb(243, 243, 243);"><h1 style="box-sizing:border-box;font-size:1em;margin:0px;"> </h1> </div><b>AC1: Migration logic</b><div><b><br></b><div><b>Given </b>Account (Vendor) records have PRM_PNC__c populated, </div><div><b>And </b>HealthcareFacility records have an AccountId lookup to the Vendor Account, </div><div><b>When </b>the migration script runs, </div><div><b>Then </b>for each HealthcareFacility: </div><div><ul><li>If an account has only one location, then PNC is checked on that location during data migration </li> </ul><div><span><b>AC2: Validation</b><br></span><div><b>Given </b>the data migration script has finished executing, </div><div><b>When </b>the Admin runs a validation query against the database, </div><span><b>Then </b>the count of HealthcareFacility records with PRM_PNC__c = true shall match (or be a superset of) the count of Vendor Accounts that had PRM_PNC__c = true and have at least one related HealthcareFacility.</span><br> </div><br> </div> </div>																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																							
