1167777	Requirement	Delegated - Data Model – Create the New "Delegated" Field			Approved by PO	Proposed	Kothapalli, Prashanth (CW) <Prashanth.Kothapalli@ibx.com>		IHG	BX; DART; FF26; PDM; QW	535116960	7803	IHG\BTS EIM\PNM\Sprint 53	9725	IHG\BTS EIM\Provider Network Management		<div><b></b> </div><span><b>Business Context (The &quot;Why&quot;)</b></span><div><span><b><br></b></span><div>Currently, a practitioner is only considered &quot;Delegated&quot; by the system if every single one of their practice locations is delegated (tracked by the legacy PRM_DelegatedOnly__c field).<br> </div><div><br> </div><span>The business rule is changing: moving forward, a practitioner should be considered &quot;Delegated&quot; if any one of their practice locations is delegated. To implement this safely and ensure a smooth cutover, we are creating a brand new field to hold this updated logic rather than modifying the old one in place.<br><br><span><b>AC1: Create the New &quot;Delegated&quot; Field</b></span></span> </div><div><span><span><b><br></b></span><div><b>Given </b>the Account object currently utilizes the legacy PRM_DelegatedOnly__c field to track delegated status,<br> </div><div><br> </div><div><b>When </b>the Admin creates the new custom field on the Account object to support the updated business rules,<br> </div><div><br> </div><div><b>Then </b>the field shall be configured exactly as follows:<br> </div><div><br> </div><div><ul><li><b>API Name</b>: PRM_Delegated__c </li><li><b>Type</b>: Checkbox </li><li><b>Label</b>: &quot;Delegated&quot; </li><li><b>Description</b>:&nbsp;Determines if the Practitioner is associated with any of the Delegated Practice Locations. </li><li><span><span><b>Field-Level Security (FLS)</b>: Must perfectly match the existing permissions of the legacy PRM_DelegatedOnly__c field so user access remains uninterrupted.</span></span> </li> </ul> </div></span><div><div><div style="box-sizing:border-box;"><span style="box-sizing:border-box;"><b style="box-sizing:border-box;">AC2: Field Access, Permission Sets, and Metadata Notification</b></span> </div><div style="box-sizing:border-box;"><span style="box-sizing:border-box;"><b style="box-sizing:border-box;"><br style="box-sizing:border-box;"></b></span> </div><blockquote style="box-sizing:border-box;margin:0px 0px 0px 40px;border:none;"><div style="box-sizing:border-box;"><div style="box-sizing:border-box;"><b style="box-sizing:border-box;">Given<span>&nbsp;</span></b>the new field has been created in Salesforce, </div> </div><b style="box-sizing:border-box;">When<span>&nbsp;</span></b>the Admin configures user access and deployment documentation,<br style="box-sizing:border-box;"><b style="box-sizing:border-box;">Then<span>&nbsp;</span></b>the access levels shall be explicitly mapped as follows:<div style="box-sizing:border-box;"><div style="box-sizing:border-box;"><br style="box-sizing:border-box;"> </div> </div><b style="box-sizing:border-box;">Read Access</b>: Credentialing, PDA, Network Management QC Permission Set<br style="box-sizing:border-box;"><b style="box-sizing:border-box;">Edit Access</b>: PRM_CredentialingUser, PRM_ProviderDataAdmin, and PRM_NetworkManagementQC<br style="box-sizing:border-box;"><b style="box-sizing:border-box;">View All, Read</b>: PRM_DataViewAll<br style="box-sizing:border-box;"><b style="box-sizing:border-box;">Read, Create, Edit, View All</b>: PRM_DataModifyAll<br style="box-sizing:border-box;"><blockquote style="box-sizing:border-box;margin:0px 0px 0px 40px;border:none;"><b style="box-sizing:border-box;"><br style="box-sizing:border-box;"></b></blockquote><div style="box-sizing:border-box;"><span style="box-sizing:border-box;">And the Admin shall explicitly NOTIFY KISHLAY + AKSHAY to add the field for SF to DART Metadata &amp; Data Dictionary.</span> </div></blockquote><span style="box-sizing:border-box;"></span><br><br> </div> </div><div> </div> </div>																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																							
1397423	Requirement	Delegated - Logic to update the new "Delegated" Field (ReCred Batch and Delegated Trigger)			Ready for Grooming	Proposed	Kothapalli, Prashanth (CW) <Prashanth.Kothapalli@ibx.com>		IHG	BX; FF26; PDM; QW	535116960	7803	IHG\BTS EIM\PNM\Sprint 53	9725	IHG\BTS EIM\Provider Network Management		<div><b></b> </div><span><b>Business Context (The &quot;Why&quot;)</b></span><div><span><b><br></b></span><div>Currently, a practitioner is only considered &quot;Delegated&quot; by the system if every single one of their practice locations is delegated (tracked by the legacy PRM_DelegatedOnly__c field).<br> </div><div><br> </div><span>The business rule is changing: moving forward, a practitioner should be considered &quot;Delegated&quot; if any one of their practice locations is delegated. To implement this safely and ensure a smooth cutover, we are creating a brand new field to hold this updated logic rather than modifying the old one in place.<br><br><span><b></b></span></span> </div><span><b>AC1: Update the Logic (delegatedOnlyPractitioner)</b></span><div><span><b><br></b></span><div><b>Given </b>the current logic initializes each practitioner as &quot;delegated&quot; and flips them to &quot;not delegated&quot; if it finds even one non-delegated facility,<br> </div><div><br> </div><div><b>When </b>the developer updates the method's logic,<br> </div><div><br> </div><div><b>Then </b>the logic shall be inverted: it must initialize practitioners as &quot;not delegated&quot; (false) and flip them to &quot;delegated&quot; (true) the moment it finds any HealthcareFacility where PRM_IsDelegated__c == true.<br> </div><span>And all references must point to the new PRM_Delegated__c field instead of the legacy PRM_DelegatedOnly__c field.<br><br><b><br></b><span><b>AC2: Update the ReCRed Batch Filter</b></span></span> </div><div><span><span><b><br></b></span><div><b>Given </b>the PRM_CheckCAQHAccessOnDueAccountsBatch query currently filters out practitioners by checking if